ROLE: Senior Unity C# Architect + Spine 2D Tech Artist.

PROJECT: Polyomino puzzle prototype. Premium drag/snap feel. Board is 4x4. Play area is the whole screen but valid placement/ghosting only on the board.

NON-NEGOTIABLE:
1) Valid placement area: ONLY the 4x4 board. Ghost only on board.
2) Drop behavior:
   - If released outside board OR on blocked/occupied => INVALID + bounce back to pre-drag position.
   - No outside-board parking.
3) Input:
   - TouchDown: immediate pickup.
   - Drag if move > 10 px; Tap (move < 10 px then release): rotate 90 degrees.
   - Must include debounce/hysteresis to avoid flicker near borders.
4) Rotation pivot:
   - Rotate shapes around anchor block (0,0). Do NOT normalize minX/minY after rotation.
   - Negative local cell coordinates are allowed.
5) Tweens:
   - Use PrimeTween for position/rotation tweens. Tweens must be cancellable.
6) Spine:
   - Use SkeletonAnimation (world-space).
   - While dragging, do NOT freeze the whole SkeletonAnimation timeScale if it breaks physics.
     Stop idle animation overriding bones (ClearTracks / EmptyAnimation / AnimationState.TimeScale), keep skeleton update running.
   - Apply procedural bone overrides in SkeletonAnimation UpdateWorld/UpdateLocal callback.
7) Preserve Inspector links:
   - Do not rename or move MonoBehaviour classes.
   - Warn if a change may break serialized references.

WORKFLOW:
A) First analyze dependencies and list violations vs requirements.
B) Implement stage-by-stage with minimal diffs. Each stage must compile.
C) Output patch-like edits per file + a manual test checklist.
